course: dictionary
lesson: 11192
title: Wistfulness: a soft kind of sad
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Wistfulness is a feeling, and it is a noun, so you can have wistfulness or look with wistfulness. Feeling words can be hard to pin down, so read the clues around them. «The two friends, so far from home themselves, had something of wistfulness in their eyes.» Being far from home is the clue: they miss home, so wistfulness is a longing for something you miss.
explain: Wistfulness is softer than grief. Grief is a deep, heavy sadness, but wistfulness is gentle and often mixed with fond memories of what you miss. Think of looking at a photo of a place you loved and wishing you could go back.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Put in longing or missing in place of wistfulness. If the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is right.
fact: Wistfulness means a gentle, sad feeling of longing for something you miss or cannot have.
fact: Wistful is the adjective: a wistful look is a look full of longing.
fact: Wistfulness is softer than grief and is often mixed with fond memories.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Mole feels wistfulness when he smells his old home in the snow.
fact: Context clue: the friends are far from home, so wistfulness is about missing home.
exercise: «The two friends, so far from home themselves, had something of wistfulness in their eyes.» What does wistfulness mean here? | Loud laughter and joy | *Gentle sadness and longing for home | Sleepiness after a long day | Great anger at the weather
exercise: Mole smells his old home in the snow. Which feeling is wistfulness? | *Gentle, sad longing for the home he misses | Happy and busy | Frightened of the snow | Cross with his friends
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to wistfulness? | *Longing | Anger | Joy | Boredom
test: Alice looks with wistfulness at the lovely garden through the tiny door. What is she feeling? | Scared of the tiny door | Cheerful about her dinner | *Longing to get into the garden she cannot reach | Bored with the garden
test: How can you check the meaning of wistfulness in a sentence? | Skip it and never return to it | Count the letters | *Put in a word like longing and see if it still makes sense | Read it aloud very fast
exam: Which best describes wistfulness? | Fast and angry | *A gentle, sad longing for something missed | A kind of sleepiness | Loud and cheerful
